### [Rapidly Excited Programmer](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/23204289/how-to-read-programmatically-a-mailcap-file-in-java/23204636#23204636) ([code](/q/23204636))

A [modified version of `mailcap.findmatch`](https://stackoverflow.com/a/23204636/2943403) that also executes the program returned by `mailcap.findmatch`.

```java
/**
 * Simulates the mailcap.findmatch function.
 * Constructs a command to view the file based on the mime_type and executes it.
 */
public static final String findmatch(String mime_type) throws Exception {
    // Check for trailing semicolons.
    while (mime_type.endsWith(";")) {
        mime_type = mime_type.substring(0, mime_type.length() - 1);
    }
    final String[] command = { "mailcap", "-l", "-v", "-" };
    final Process mailcap = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);
    final BufferedReader in =
        new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(mailcap.getInputStream()));
    while (true) {
        final String line = in.readLine();
        if (line == null) {
            break;
        }
        if (line.toLowerCase().contains(mime_type.toLowerCase())) {
            final String mime_line = in.readLine();
            if (mime_line!= null) {
                final String result = mime_line.split(":", 2)[1];
                return result;
            }
        }
    }
    // Return null if no result has been found.
    return null;
}

