# PHTF

Code injection and XSS exercises. The questions ask you to add a code injection hole in the provided code and an XSS flaw in the user generated input. These are then presented to a code checker, which returns a grade (0 to 3 stars). In the course, you are instructed to exploit the vulnerability, so that the grade gets 3 stars.

The code for each exercise can be found inside each `/exercise` subdirectory and the respective assignment is stated at the top in the file. The code checker is at `/checker.py` and the code checker-client is in `client.js`.

In case you want to run the checker without installing the client, you can just run the script in `/checker.py`. There's also a `start_check_server` Python script, that simply starts up a webserver at port 20200.

## Getting started

In case you don't have Python installed on your machine (or use OSX), you can install it using Homebrew by running

``` sh
brew install Python3
```

Next, install npm using the instructions at https://nodejs.org/en/download/package-manager/ and then install the client by navigating to `/phtf_grader_client` and running

``` sh
npm install
```

Now, you should be ready to test the checker

