# JudgeProblemGenerator

A program used for generating Judge Problems.

A problem consists of two parts, the assistant part and the user part. The assistant part should be placed *before* (or *at the same time as*) the user part.

The assistant part should be a Java snippet (or any other programming language's code snippet). It tells your program which file path is given to your program as a command line argument (the first element is the program name so this element should not be considered in the snippet). The Java snippet and the first non-whitespace character of user part should not conflict.

The user part is a snippet of your code, which should be as close as possible to what the actual problem would be if it were just a Java snippet.

The snippet of your whole program after your name (equivalent to *header* in a normal programming language) should be on its own.
The snippet can be a single line statement as long as we don't see anything below it.

The **program name** is the first argument on the command line.

## Usage
```shell
java -jar JudgeProblemGenerator.jar [output path]
```
