## Exercise 4: Insecure DEserialization in a Server

This exercise demonstrates an issue in Java libraries/frameworks with the potential to unserialize arbitrary code.

## Task 1: Understanding the issue

Take a look at the following server implementation that does not properly sanitize inputs and uses libraries that can deserialize arbitrary code:

- [source](app/src/main/java/io/github/secB11/javasecurity/deserialization/server/)
- [web page](app/#/challenge/deserialization?task=1)
- [applet](app/)
- [example](example/src/main/java/io/github/secB11/javasecurity/example/deserialization/server/)
- [example applet](example/app/src/main/java/io/github/secB11/javasecurity/example/deserialization/)

## Task 2: Solving the issue

Your mission is to unserialize arbitrary code on the server side by creating an XXE attack, which we will call XXE-DDos attack. You are free to modify the code for it to be easier or harder, however you need to adhere to the following specifications:

